module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.TorusCharacterGZeroAction
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFiniteType
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Proper
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FiniteType
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.ClosedImmersion
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.OpenImmersion
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.TorusInvariantAffineFiltration

/-! # Character annihilation on the nonfixed torus complement

Source: agent-formulated supporting statement for Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017),
Section 22d, Theorem 22.50, p.480. Milne invokes Nielsen (1974) and Iversen (1976),
9.4; it does not state this concentration prerequisite. Thomason (1986), nonfixed-locus
character annihilation, is marked WANTED in the DAG.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-torus-nonfixed-complement-annihilation)

The fixed-locus condition tests all commutative algebras and all further algebra
extensions. The open complement carries its induced action. The existing integral
equivariant coherent group is used, with its character-twist action normalized by
`IsCharacterAction`. No smoothness, properness or reduced-stabilizer assumption occurs.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory Opposite
open scoped CategoryTheory.MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.EquivariantCoherent

/-- Every integral equivariant coherent class on the nonfixed complement is killed
by a finite product of factors `1 - e^χ` with nonzero group-scheme characters.

Source: agent-formulated concentration prerequisite for Milne (2017), Section 22d,
Theorem 22.50, p.480; Thomason (1986), nonfixed-locus annihilation (WANTED).
(blueprint: lem-sfb-torus-nonfixed-complement-annihilation)

Proof, following the accepted seven-step DAG split:
1. Apply lem-sfb-torus-invariant-affine-filtration to U. Its reduction has a finite
   invariant closed filtration with affine strata. A fixed point of a stratum would
   map into both W and its disjoint complement U, so every stratum has empty fixed functor.
2. On an affine stratum Spec A choose Laurent coordinates on T. Coassociativity gives
   a homogeneous expansion a = sum a_m with coaction a_m maps to z^m tensor a_m;
   multiplication adds degrees, including for nonreduced A.
3. The ideal generated by all nonzero-degree components represents the fixed functor:
   Laurent coefficient comparison works over every test algebra. Its quotient is the
   zero ring, so finitely many nonzero-weight semi-invariants f_i generate the unit ideal.
4. Filter Spec A by the successive ideals (f_1,...,f_i). On each open difference f_i
   is invertible. Multiplication by f_i gives M isomorphic to its forward character
   twist because f_i(ty) = χ_i(t) f_i(y). Thus 1-e^χ_i kills that difference's group.
5. Apply lem-sfb-equivariant-coherent-localization-sequence down this finite chain.
   Exactness lifts a class killed on the open to the closed term. Character linearity
   then multiplies the previous annihilator by 1-e^χ_i. Start with the empty term,
   annihilated by the empty product 1.
6. Repeat this descending localization induction for the finite affine-stratum
   filtration. The same localization sequence for U_red into U has empty complement,
   hence gives a surjection. Lift α and push its annihilation forward. No assertion
   of injectivity or nilpotent invariance is needed.
7. If r=0 or U is empty, α=0 and n=0 works. In characteristic p the action t.x=t^p x
   on G_m uses the nonzero character p and the factor 1-e^p, even with stabilizer μ_p.
   All groups and coefficients remain integral. -/
theorem torus_nonfixed_complement_annihilation
    (F : Type u) [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F] (r : ℕ)
    (T : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F))))
    (hT : Nonempty (T ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus F r))
    (Y U : CategoryTheory.Mod (Over (Spec (.of F))) T.X)
    [IsSeparated Y.X.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType Y.X.hom] [QuasiCompact Y.X.hom]
    (W : Over (Spec (.of F))) (i : W ⟶ Y.X) [IsClosedImmersion i.left]
    (hfixed : ∀ (A : CommAlgCat.{u} F)
      (y : (algSpec (.of F)).obj (op A) ⟶ Y.X),
      (∃ w : (algSpec (.of F)).obj (op A) ⟶ W, w ≫ i = y) ↔
        ∀ (B : CommAlgCat.{u} F) (f : A ⟶ B)
          (t : (algSpec (.of F)).obj (op B) ⟶ T.X),
          t • ((algSpec (.of F)).map f.op ≫ y) = (algSpec (.of F)).map f.op ≫ y)
    (j : U ⟶ Y) [IsOpenImmersion j.hom.left]
    (hcomplement : Set.range j.hom.left = (Set.range i.left)ᶜ)
    (D : ActionGroupoidModel T.X U.X)
    [m : Module (TrivialTorusCoherent.CharacterRing T) (GZero D)]
    (hm : IsCharacterAction D m) (α : GZero D) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (χs : Fin n → TrivialTorusCoherent.Character T),
      (∀ k, χs k ≠ 0) ∧
        (∏ k, (1 - AddMonoidAlgebra.single (χs k) 1 :
          TrivialTorusCoherent.CharacterRing T)) • α = 0 := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.EquivariantCoherent
